# Local development only. Vite loads this automatically in dev mode.
#
# Committed on purpose: these point at the containers in docker-compose.dev.yml
# and contain no secrets — a public OIDC client id is public by definition.
# Without them `pnpm dev` starts, serves a blank page, and fails in the console
# with "VITE_OIDC_ISSUER was not set", which is a poor first impression of a
# working checkout.
#
# Production values are baked in at image build time from the root .env — see
# docker-compose.yml (service: web). Vite inlines them, so changing the public
# URL requires a rebuild, not a restart.

# Relative on purpose. Vite proxies /api to the API (see vite.config.ts), which
# keeps every request same-origin — exactly as Caddy does in production.
#
# An absolute http://localhost:3100/api would bypass the proxy and make these
# cross-origin. The API enables no CORS at all, deliberately, so the browser
# blocks the response and every screen fails with "Failed to fetch".
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api

# Dev Keycloak runs start-dev with no relative path, so there is no /auth prefix
# here — production has one. The redirect URIs for this origin are registered in
# ops/keycloak/realm-hr.json.
VITE_OIDC_ISSUER=http://localhost:8080/realms/hr
VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=hr-system
